 Model Variants
 Free Variant
 Copy page Copy page 
 Access free models with the :free variant
 Copy page Copy page 
 The :free variant allows you to access free versions of models on OpenRouter. 
 ​ 
 Usage 
 Append :free to the ID of a model that has a free entry. :free is a catalog variant , so the free version appears as its own entry in the models API with its own pricing, context length, and endpoints, and only models that list one support it: 
 { 
 "model" : "meta-llama/llama-3.2-3b-instruct:free" 
 } 
 ​ 
 Details 
 Free variants provide access to models without cost, but may have different rate limits or availability compared to paid versions. 
 Fallbacks to paid models are billed If you list a :free model in a models fallback array , OpenRouter tries the next model in the array when the free model is rate-limited, unavailable, or has no endpoint that supports your request. Each model is billed at its own price, so a fallback to a paid model incurs charges even though the first model was :free . To keep a request free, list only :free models in models , or use the Free Models Router ( openrouter/free ) on its own, which falls back only to other free models. 
 ​ 
 Related Resources 
 Free Models Router - Learn how to use the Free Models Router in the Chat Playground for zero-cost inference
